Chapter 4 — Temporal Logic Preliminaries

4.1 Operators

Standard LTL: \Box, \Diamond, \bigcirc, \mathcal{U}. Bounded variants: \Box_{[0,T]}, \Diamond_{[0,T]}.

4.2 Safety and Invariance

Definition 4.1. A safety property states nothing bad ever happens. It is falsifiable by a finite trace.

Definition 4.2. An invariance is \Box \varphi.

4.3 Clock Reduction for Bounded Invariance

Proposition 4.1. A bounded invariance \Box_{[0,T]} \varphi is equivalent to an ordinary invariance \Box \varphi' with \varphi' = (t - t_0 \leq T) \Rightarrow \varphi, where t_0 is a persistent entry timestamp.

Proof. The clock t is monotone; t - t_0 increases without reset. The bounded operator is expressible as a state predicate. \square

This reduction is used in Chapter 12. The crucial constraint, fixed in V1.2: t_0 is non-resettable by any KSI action.

