Chapter 5 — State Machine

5.1 State Components

s = \langle \Gamma, \Pi, \operatorname{Rev}, \operatorname{Exec}, \operatorname{Pend}, \operatorname{Int}, t_0, \mathcal{A}, t \rangle

where:

· \Gamma : A \to \mathcal{P}_{\downarrow}(\mathcal{C});
· \Pi \in \Pi^{\ast};
· \operatorname{Rev} : A \times \mathcal{C} \to \mathbb{B};
· \operatorname{Exec}, \operatorname{Pend} \subseteq A \times \mathcal{O};
· \operatorname{Int} \in \mathcal{I};
· t_0 \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} \cup \{\bot\} is the intervention entry timestamp (persistent, non-resettable);
· \mathcal{A} is the audit record;
· t \in \mathbb{R}_{\geq 0} is the global clock.

5.2 Intervention States

\mathcal{I} = \{ \text{Normal}, \text{Reduced}, \text{OversightRequired}, \text{SafeHalt} \}.

Chain: \text{Normal} \to \text{Reduced} \to \text{OversightRequired} \to \text{SafeHalt}.

5.3 Effective Authority

Definition 5.1.

\operatorname{Auth}(a) = \bigcup_{c \in \Gamma(a)} \operatorname{desc}(c).

5.4 Policy Bound

Definition 5.2. \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\pi}(a) \subseteq \mathcal{C}.

5.5 Initial State

s_0 satisfies:

· \Pi = \pi_0, explicitly authorized;
· \Gamma(a) \subseteq \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\pi_0}(a);
· \operatorname{Rev}(a, c) = \bot;
· \operatorname{Exec} = \operatorname{Pend} = \emptyset;
· \operatorname{Int} = \text{Normal};
· t_0 = \bot;
· t = 0;
· \mathcal{A} initialized per audit model.

