Chapter 6 — Transition Relation

6.1 Actions

Each action is a predicate on (s, s').

Request. \operatorname{Request}(a, o): modifies \operatorname{Pend} only.

Grant. \operatorname{Grant}(a, c):

c \in \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\Pi}(a) \land \operatorname{Authorized}(a, c) \land \neg \operatorname{Rev}(a, c).

Delegate. \operatorname{Delegate}(a, b, c_{\text{parent}}, c_{\text{child}}):

c_{\text{child}} \sqsubseteq c_{\text{parent}} \land c_{\text{parent}} \in \Gamma(a) \land \operatorname{delegable}(c_{\text{parent}}) \land b \in \operatorname{authorizedDelegees}(a).

Revoke. \operatorname{Revoke}(a, c): installs \operatorname{Rev}(a, c) = \top and cascades to \operatorname{cascade}(a, c) atomically.

Execute. \operatorname{Execute}(a, o): requires \operatorname{Commit}(a, o, s) = \text{permit}.

UpdatePolicy. \operatorname{UpdatePolicy}(\pi):

\operatorname{ValidGovernanceAuthorization}(\pi) \land \operatorname{UpdateValidation}(\pi).

Intervene. \operatorname{Intervene}(i):

i \in \operatorname{allowed}(\operatorname{Int}) \land \operatorname{scope}(i) \subseteq \operatorname{scope}(\operatorname{Int}) \land \operatorname{duration}(i) \leq T_{\max}.

Recover. \operatorname{Recover}(\rho): requires \operatorname{IndependentAuthorization}(\rho).

Tick. \operatorname{Tick}(\epsilon): t' = t + \epsilon, t' \geq t.

6.2 Frame Condition

For each \alpha:

\alpha(s, s') \Longrightarrow \bigwedge_{v \notin \operatorname{wr}(\alpha)} v' = v.

6.3 Fairness

Weak fairness on the enforcement boundary only.

