Chapter 8 — The Inductive Invariant Framework

8.1 The Corrected Privilege-Safety Proof Obligation

Version 1.1's Theorem 14.1 was incomplete. Delegation non-amplification constrains only delegated capabilities. It does not establish that initially held capabilities are within bound, nor that all transitions preserve the bound.

Version 1.2 proves preservation by induction over every transition.

8.2 The Invariant I-1 (Privilege Bounds)

I_1(s) \;:\Longleftrightarrow\; \forall a \in A : \operatorname{Auth}(a) \subseteq \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\Pi}(a).

8.3 Induction Scheme

Init. I_1(s_0) holds by the initial-state predicate.

Preservation. For every action \alpha and every s, s' with \alpha(s, s') and I_1(s), prove I_1(s').

8.4 Case Analysis

Request. Does not modify \Gamma. I_1 preserved trivially.

Grant. Adds c with c \in \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\Pi}(a). Since \operatorname{Auth} is the union of downward closures, and c \in \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\Pi}(a), the union remains in \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\Pi}(a) (given \operatorname{MaxAuth} is downward closed under \sqsubseteq, which is a modeling assumption stated explicitly).

Delegate. By Theorem 7.1, c_{\text{child}} \sqsubseteq c_{\text{parent}} \in \Gamma(a) \subseteq \operatorname{Auth}(a) \subseteq \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\Pi}(a). Adding c_{\text{child}} to \Gamma(b) preserves the bound.

Revoke. Removes capabilities. \operatorname{Auth} shrinks. Preservation trivial.

Execute. Does not modify \Gamma. Preservation trivial.

UpdatePolicy. This is the critical case, addressed in Chapter 9.

Intervene. Does not modify \Gamma of cognitive agents. For KSI agents, see I-6.

Recover. Does not modify \Gamma.

8.5 The Policy-Update Case

Assumption 8.1 (Policy monotonicity under update). Either:

· (a) \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\pi'}(a) = \operatorname{MaxAuth}_{\pi}(a) for all a (no policy effect on bounds), or
· (b) the policy update is accompanied by a revocation sweep that removes any capability now outside bound, executed atomically with the policy change.

Without (a) or (b), I-1 may fail on policy update. Version 1.2 states this explicitly.

