Chapter 11 — Bounded Intervention Theory

11.1 The V1.1 Defect

Version 1.1 stated only that Intervene sets \operatorname{duration}(i) \leq T_{\max}. This does not prevent repeated interventions, clock resets, or recovery transitions from circumventing the bound.

11.2 The Persistent Timestamp

Constraint 11.1 (Non-resettable entry). When \operatorname{Int} transitions from Normal to any non-Normal state, t_0 is set to t. No KSI action modifies t_0 except to reset it to \bot when \operatorname{Int} returns to Normal.

Constraint 11.2 (No reset without return). t_0 cannot be updated while \operatorname{Int} \neq \text{Normal}.

11.3 Bounded Intervention Invariant

Invariant I-5 (Bounded intervention).

\Box \; \left( \operatorname{Int} \neq \text{Normal} \Longrightarrow t - t_0 \leq T_{\max} \right).

Proof obligation.

· Init. t_0 = \bot, so the antecedent is false. Trivial.
· Intervene. Sets t_0 = t, so t - t_0 = 0 \leq T_{\max}.
· Tick. Increases t. Preservation requires that if t - t_0 = T_{\max}, no further Tick is permitted while \operatorname{Int} \neq \text{Normal}.
· Recover. Returns to Normal, setting t_0 = \bot. Trivial.

11.4 The Deadline Expiration Problem

When t - t_0 = T_{\max} and the threat remains unresolved, safety and automatic expiration conflict. The dissertation must state the fallback.

Constraint 11.3 (Fallback policy). At deadline, one of:

· (a) transition to SafeHalt and require human authorization for any further action;
· (b) block all non-Normal operations and require independent authorization for continued intervention;
· (c) permit a single bounded extension only via an independent authorization event, with the extension recorded and bounded.

The fallback is a policy parameter, not a theorem. The invariant I-5 holds regardless of which fallback is chosen, provided the fallback does not itself reset t_0 without independent authorization.

11.5 No Self-Renewal

Proposition 11.1. The KSI cannot renew its own deadline.

Proof. By Constraint 11.2, only external authorization can extend t_0. \square

11.6 Scope Non-Expansion

Proposition 11.2.

\operatorname{Intervene}(i) \Longrightarrow \operatorname{scope}(i) \subseteq \operatorname{scope}(\operatorname{Int}).

Proof. Precondition of Intervene. \square

11.7 No Self-Expansion

Invariant I-6 (No self-expansion).

\Box \; \forall a \in A_{\text{KSI}} : \operatorname{Auth}(a) \subseteq \operatorname{Auth}_{\text{granted}}(a).

Proof obligation. Write sets of all KSI actions exclude the KSI authority-grant mechanism. \square

11.8 Detection ≠ Authority

Invariant I-7 (Detection ≠ authority).

\Box \; \forall a \in A_{\text{KSI}} : \operatorname{Detects}(a, \text{threat}) \Longrightarrow \neg \operatorname{HasAuthority}(a, \text{intervene})

unless \operatorname{Authorized}(a, \text{intervene}) holds independently.

Proof obligation. Detection actions do not modify \Gamma. \square

11.9 Novelty Statement

Bounded intervention (I-5, I-6, I-7) is the dissertation's most defensible novel contribution. The fixed I-5 with persistent non-resettable t_0 is the corrected form.

