J.7 Revocation Cascade

```
   Before revocation:

   Γ(a) = { c_parent, c_x, c_y }
   Rev(a, ·) = ∅

   Revocation event: Rev(a, c_parent) ← ⊤

   ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────┐
   │  cascade(a, c_parent) = { c' : c' ⊑ c_parent}│
   │                                             │
   │    c_parent                                 │
   │      ├── c_x   ◄── descendant               │
   │      └── c_y   ◄── descendant               │
   └─────────────────────────────────────────────┘

   After atomic installation:

   Γ(a) = Γ(a) \ cascade(a, c_parent)
        = { }              (all descendants removed)

   Rev(a, c_parent) = ⊤
   Rev(a, c_x)      = ⊤
   Rev(a, c_y)      = ⊤

   Atomic linearization point T_r:
   ─────────────────────────────────► time
                │
                │ Revoked at T_r
                │
   Any operation o with relies(o, c') for c' ∈ cascade
   and T_e(o) > T_r  ⟹  Commit(a,o,s) ≠ permit
```

